  "meaning_guidance": "Describe only entities and relationships entailed by the supplied claims. Type each entity by what it is: places/devices/systems/organisms are physical; material, energy and signal are carriers that move or are converted, never route endpoints. A counted collection is its own system entity, distinct from its members. Cite every claim an entity takes part in. Include separate source-named processes and unspecific energy when a claim explicitly states them. Omit ungrounded entities. flows_to moves the carrier between two physical endpoints, optionally via a distinct physical device; attach its driving process to flows_to.process if the source names one; electricity can power a pump and a device or process can produce an output, but the input cannot create the material being moved. Cite all claims needed for each fact. Give each measured claim the entity it actually counts or measures, or null; never turn a count into heights or percentages. Use the smallest set of directly supported facts that conveys the source; a nearby device, later process or familiar technology does not by itself justify an extra connection, output, or causal fact. Do not invent a link simply to use every entity. Use the complete accepted combined-process entity for a source-stated joint cause; its individual constituents do not each independently cause the outcome. When alignment explicitly names the direction of something, target that literal direction concept, not the field or material whose direction it describes.",
